# Evidence: one current synthesis. Earlier dated text stays in Updates/source editions.
evidence=page_intro('Evidence & open questions','What is established?<br>What still needs a test?','Finite mathematical checks, constructor executions and physical measurements answer different questions. The programme has no promoted physical identification.')
evidence+='<div class="status-strip"><div>Physical promotion <b>0</b></div><div>Independent review <b>Scope-specific / pending or HOLD</b></div></div>'
evidence+=chapter('01','Assess each result at its own level.','<div class="atlas-evidence-levels"><div><span>01 / Mathematics</span><h3>A declared finite object</h3><p>Exact algebra or a scoped proof on a specified carrier, metric and source convention.</p></div><div><span>02 / Computation</span><h3>A reproducible execution</h3><p>A frozen numerical or exact record with input hashes, tolerances and failure controls.</p></div><div><span>03 / Review</span><h3>An attributable challenge</h3><p>A non-constructor return bound to the exact claim or package, with its independence and scope.</p></div><div><span>04 / Correspondence</span><h3>An eligible physical test</h3><p>A calibrated map, units, uncertainty, baseline and a frozen independent acceptance rule.</p></div></div><p>The CRL-2 source proposal is preserved as a proposal. Publishing this hierarchy does not enact it or promote a scientific status.</p>'+actions(('/sources/?id=A21','Read the source proposal'),('/reconciliation/','Inspect source dispositions')))
evidence+=chapter('02','Current programme boundaries.','<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Programme</th><th>What the current record supports</th><th>What remains open</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Source, events and refinement</td><td>Conditional finite mechanisms, exact compatibility and nonselection results</td><td>Native source selection, preparation and a physical time/observable map</td></tr><tr id="observation-review-status"><td>Observation and estimation</td><td>Finite observability results and constructor certificates on declared records</td><td>Attributable external replay, uniform guarantees where claimed and physical metrology; review HOLD preserved</td></tr><tr><td>Action and stability</td><td>Declared action, scoped stability results and conditional preparation/error budgets</td><td>Realization and records meeting the complete experiment contract</td></tr><tr><td>Parity transport</td><td>Finite selected sector, typed transport identities and prospective numeric admission</td><td>Non-constructor review of the new contract, original attributable approval/raw output gaps and physical parity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>'+actions(('/research/','Read the programme map'),('/research-record/','Inspect the source-bound returns')))
evidence+=chapter('03','A concrete bridge candidate, with a data boundary.','<div id="measurable-audit-v01"><p>A rank-one rotor–matter circuit emulator was selected for development. The published LC device is a partial benchmark: its oscillator links and chain do not implement the full UD Hamiltonian and required diamonds.</p><p>No audited dataset supplies every preparation, energy and source-work gate. The next proposed component experiment is a closed-diamond test with a calibrated measurement contract.</p>'+grid(link('/evidence/measurable-audit/','Read the realization and dataset audit','Selection, inspected records, mismatches and minimum experiment requirements.'))+'</div>')
evidence+=chapter('04','Read historical replication claims with their receipts.','<p>The historical parity record reports 12 in-scope passes and six failing controls from external-AI replication, with the permanent rider <em>transport consistency, not dynamical discovery</em>. Receipt linkage and the full ruling document are recovered; named or signed original approval and the raw-output commitment remain unresolved.</p><p>This is a source-recorded internal transport result. It is not independent-human review or a laboratory measurement, and the new prospective contract does not retroactively revise the old scores.</p>'+actions(('/research/parity/','Read the parity programme'),('/research-record/#custody','Inspect source and review custody')))
evidence+=chapter('05','What a physical return must contain.','<ol class="atlas-sequence"><li><strong>State the correspondence.</strong><span>Define the mathematical object, measured observable, units and calibration.</span></li><li><strong>Freeze the test.</strong><span>Specify baseline, exclusions, uncertainty budget, acceptance and failure rules before target exposure.</span></li><li><strong>Separate the evaluation.</strong><span>Record target custody, reviewer independence, negative results and the exact supported scope.</span></li></ol>'+actions(('/contribution/','Choose a review or experiment gate'),('/archive/','Find the underlying evidence')))
evidence+=chapter('06','Applied programmes have separate evidence ledgers.',grid(link('https://mqm-research.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/','MQM','Fault-aware quantum-code and controller research; hardware advantage needs its own evidence.'),link('https://voxifold-systems.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/','Lattix Systems','Spatial compute; equal-recall, equal-hardware benchmarks remain separate.')))
